# SafeSphere Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values.
# NEVER commit .env.local – it contains your real API keys.
#
# ── Option A: quick local test of sign-up / password-reset emails ──
# 1. npm run dev  →  app is at http://localhost:3000 (see vite.config.ts)
# 2. Supabase → Authentication → URL configuration:
#    Site URL: http://localhost:3000
#    Redirect URLs: add http://localhost:3000 and http://localhost:3000/**
# 3. Authentication → Emails: ensure SMTP or default provider sends mail
# 4. Authentication → URL Configuration: Site URL and Redirect URLs must include your app
#    origin with a trailing slash (e.g. http://localhost:3000/ and http://localhost:3000/**)
#    so sign-up confirmation and password-reset links work.
# 5. For a confirmation code in email, keep "Confirm email" enabled for sign-up (Auth settings in dashboard).
# 6. Register with a real inbox; use Forgot password to test the reset link (a popup asks for the new password).

# Supabase (required for online mode - dual offline/online storage)
# Get these from your Supabase project: Project Settings → API
# URL must be your project URL, e.g. https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
# Do NOT use https://www.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# Optional CARTO basemap key for the Live Command Map light/dark styles.
# Get one at https://carto.com/basemaps/apikey/ and restrict it to your app domains.
# Without it, SafeSphere uses the OpenStreetMap standard tile fallback.
# VITE_CARTO_BASEMAP_KEY=your_carto_basemap_key

# Required in the browser when Supabase → Authentication → Attack Protection uses captcha.
# Use the same provider as in the dashboard (Turnstile OR hCaptcha). Prefer a single key; if both VITE_ keys
# are set, the app uses hCaptcha first. Restart the dev server after changing.
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=your_turnstile_site_key
# hCaptcha: add localhost and 127.0.0.1 under Site hostnames or getcaptcha returns 403 locally.
# VITE_HCAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=your_hcaptcha_site_key
# If you see sitekey-secret-mismatch: the SECRET in Attack Protection must pair with that site key — not fixed by Redirect URLs.

# Optional: Gemini API (for AI Safety Assistant in Chat)
# VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY is required - Vite only exposes VITE_ prefixed vars to the browser
# Get your key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Optional: Core Web Vitals (CLS, INP, LCP, FCP, TTFB) for public UX monitoring.
# POST JSON body { schema, name, value, rating, delta, id, navigationType, path }.
# Your endpoint must enable CORS for your origin. Mention in your privacy policy if you log data.
# VITE_WEB_VITALS_ENDPOINT=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co/functions/v1/collect-web-vitals
# VITE_WEB_VITALS_DEBUG=1

# ── Supabase Edge Function Secrets (set via `supabase secrets set`) ──
# These are NOT VITE_ vars — they live on the Supabase server, not in the browser.
# Putting RESEND_API_KEY in this file or .env.local does NOT send email; the Edge
# Function reads secrets from Supabase only. See README → Registration confirmation.
#
# Email confirmation (Resend) — used by send-confirmation-email Edge Function
# (run: supabase secrets set RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxx)
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxx
#
# SMS confirmation (Twilio) — used by send-confirmation-sms Edge Function
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=ACxxxxxxxxxx
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=xxxxxxxxxx
# TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=+1xxxxxxxxxx
